<title>UK: BOE forecasts 1.2 bln stg shortage, offers help.</title>
<headline>BOE forecasts 1.2 bln stg shortage, offers help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England offered the UK money market an early round of assistance after forecasting a liquidity shortage of around 1.2 billion stg.</p>
<p>The operations will comprise a repo to June 11 and 12, and outright offers of bills maturing on or before June 12.</p>
<p>The Bank has provided liquidity totalling 1.175 billion stg so far on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
